# The 7-Minute Workout, Talked Through
@description The classic circuit of twelve exercises, thirty seconds each, with the talking done
  in rest chapters: each rest explains the exercise after it, so the thirty seconds of work have
  only the tones and a cue or two. You need a wall and a sturdy chair. Push-ups and crunches ask
  for your count. For a
  countdown into each exercise, choose 3-2-1 in Settings, End of Rest.
@minimum gap 0:00.8
@workout hiit
@artwork ../images/seven-minute.jpg

@include ../shared/sounds.overtone

// Each rest chapter explains what's next. Overtone plays the End of Rest beeps chosen in Settings
// after it, so the exercise starts on the go tone.

## Jumping jacks, explained
@rest
The seven-minute workout, talked through. Twelve exercises, thirty seconds each. In between, I'll
explain the next one, so while you work you only need to move.

First, jumping jacks. Jump the feet out wide as the arms go overhead, then back in. Stay light.

## Jumping jacks
--- 0:30
0:00 [go]
0:15 Halfway. Light feet.
-0:05 Five seconds.
---
[stop]

## Wall sit, explained
@rest
Breathe. Next, the wall sit. Back flat against the wall, and slide down until the knees are at a
right angle, as if sitting on a chair that isn't there. Weight in the heels.

## Wall sit
--- 0:30
0:00 [go]
0:15 Halfway. Thighs level.
-0:05 Five seconds.
---
[stop]

## Push-ups, explained
@rest
Shake out the legs. Next, push-ups. Hands under the shoulders, body straight from head to heels.
Lower the chest close to the floor. Count them: I'll ask for the number after.

## Push-ups
@track Reps
--- 0:30
0:00 [go]
0:15 Halfway. Knees down if you need to.
-0:05 Five seconds.
---
[stop]

## Crunches, explained
@rest
Good. Next, crunches. On your back, knees bent, feet flat, hands by your ears. Lift the shoulders,
not the neck, and breathe out as you rise. Count these too.

## Crunches
@track Reps
--- 0:30
0:00 [go]
0:15 Halfway. Breathe out as you lift.
-0:05 Five seconds.
---
[stop]

## Step-ups, explained
@rest
Stand up and find the chair. Next, step-ups. Step up onto the seat with one foot, bring the other up
to stand tall, then step down the same way. Switch the leading leg halfway.

## Step-ups
--- 0:30
0:00 [go]
0:15 Halfway. Lead with the other leg.
-0:05 Five seconds.
---
[stop]

## Squats, explained
@rest
Step down and breathe. Next, squats. Feet shoulder-width apart, toes turned out a little. Sit back as
if into a chair, chest up, then push through the heels to stand.

## Squats
--- 0:30
0:00 [go]
0:15 Halfway. Chest up.
-0:05 Five seconds.
---
[stop]

## Triceps dips, explained
@rest
Back to the chair. Next, triceps dips. Sit on the edge, hands beside the hips, then slide forward
off the seat. Bend the elbows straight back to lower the hips, and push back up.

## Triceps dips
--- 0:30
0:00 [go]
0:15 Halfway. Elbows back, not out.
-0:05 Five seconds.
---
[stop]

## Plank, explained
@rest
Shake out the arms. Next, the plank. Forearms on the floor, elbows under the shoulders. Squeeze the glutes and
brace the stomach, so the body is one straight line.

## Plank
--- 0:30
0:00 [go]
0:15 Halfway. Hips level.
-0:05 Five seconds.
---
[stop]

## High knees, explained
@rest
Stand and shake out. Next, high knees. Run on the spot, each knee up to hip height, on the balls of
the feet, arms pumping. It's short, so go hard.

## High knees
--- 0:30
0:00 [go]
0:15 Halfway. Drive the arms.
-0:05 Five seconds.
---
[stop]

## Lunges, explained
@rest
Next, lunges. Step forward and lower until both knees are at a right angle, the back knee just
above the floor. Push back up and switch legs. Chest tall.

## Lunges
--- 0:30
0:00 [go]
0:15 Halfway. Front knee over the ankle.
-0:05 Five seconds.
---
[stop]

## Push-up and rotation, explained
@rest
Down to the floor. Next, push-up and rotation. Do a push-up, then turn onto one hand into a side
plank, the other arm reaching for the ceiling. Back down, push-up, and turn the other way.

## Push-up and rotation
--- 0:30
0:00 [go]
0:15 Halfway. Hips high as you turn.
-0:05 Five seconds.
---
[stop]

## Side plank, explained
@rest
Last one: the side plank. On one forearm, elbow under the shoulder, feet stacked. Lift the hips so
the body is straight from head to heels. I'll tell you when to switch sides.

## Side plank
--- 0:30
0:00 [go]
0:15 Switch sides.
-0:05 Five seconds.
---
[stop]

## Cool-down
@rest
That's the seven minutes. Well done. Walk around for a minute and let your breathing settle, then
stretch the thighs and the chest.

